Scroll wheel                                    RISC OS on Linux
============
Configure's Scroll wheel chooses which way the mouse's scroll wheel (or
a trackpad's two-finger scroll) scrolls windows:

  Normal     the wheel turned away from you (or two fingers moved up)
             scrolls up, as RISC OS has always done
  Reversed   the other way round: "natural" scrolling, as on a Mac or
             a phone (the window follows your fingers)

Set uses it at once and keeps it in Choices:KVMWheel for the next start.
From the command line: *KVMWheel Reverse, *KVMWheel Normal.

